#  webkit-wpe-dark-mode-runtime.patch: runtime prefers-color-scheme switch.
#  The legacy libwpe build hardwires SystemSettings darkMode to false, so
#  websites always saw prefers-color-scheme: light. Exports
#  wpe_sfos_set_dark_mode(int) for the embedder (browser wires it to the
#  color_scheme dconf setting / Sailfish ambience) and gives ViewLegacy the
#  ViewPlatform SystemSettings observer so live pages re-evaluate their
#  color scheme without a reload.
#
# ---
Runtime dark-mode (prefers-color-scheme) switch for the legacy WPE API.

The legacy (libwpe/WPEBackend-fdo) build has no platform settings backend:
SystemSettingsManagerProxy::darkMode() is hardwired to false, so
PageClientImpl::effectiveAppearanceIsDark() is always false and every website
sees prefers-color-scheme: light, whatever the Sailfish ambience looks like.
(The upstream runtime path only exists for ENABLE(WPE_PLATFORM) via
WPESettings, and for GTK via GtkSettings.)

Three pieces:

1. wpe_sfos_set_dark_mode(int) — exported C entry point the embedder (the
   Atlantic browser UI process) calls when its color-scheme setting or the
   ambience changes. It stores darkMode into the global WebCore::SystemSettings
   (the source of truth for effectiveAppearanceIsDark() and for the
   useDarkAppearance creation parameter of new/relaunched web processes) and
   broadcasts the change to running web processes.

2. WKWPE::ViewLegacy now registers the same SystemSettings observer
   ViewPlatform already has, so live pages get
   WebPageProxy::effectiveAppearanceDidChange() -> SetUseColorAppearance and
   re-evaluate prefers-color-scheme immediately, without a reload.

3. The fallback SystemSettingsManagerProxy::darkMode() reports the current
   SystemSettings value instead of false, so the settingsDidChange() run when
   the first web view initializes the proxy cannot clobber a dark mode the
   embedder set before that.

Browser side: apps/core/settingmanager.cpp wires this to the
/apps/atlantic-browser/settings/color_scheme dconf key (light / dark /
follow ambience) and the ambience state reported by the QML root.
